{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"基础：新工具的动机与原料","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/stochastic-calculus/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"why-stochastic-calculus","title":"为何随机微积分：当路径处处不可导","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/stochastic-calculus/foundations/why-stochastic-calculus","wordCount":1560,"readingTime":7},{"seq":2,"slug":"brownian-motion","title":"布朗运动：随机微积分唯一的积分子","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/stochastic-calculus/foundations/brownian-motion","wordCount":1469,"readingTime":6},{"seq":3,"slug":"martingales","title":"鞅与过滤：随机微积分证明的语言","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/stochastic-calculus/foundations/martingales","wordCount":1373,"readingTime":6}],"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"基础-新工具的动机与原料\">基础：新工具的动机与原料</h1><p>在写下任何一个随机积分之前，必须先说服自己两件事：一是普通微积分为什么在这里失效，二是我们打算拿什么原料替代它。这一章回答的正是这两个「为什么」和「用什么」。</p>\n<p>第一篇《为何随机微积分》从一条布朗路径处处不可导的事实出发，解释 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">dt/dt</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">d</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">t</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">d</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">t</span></span></span></span></span> 失效的根源，并给出贯穿全 hub 的那句核心直觉——<span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≈</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">dW^2 \\approx dt</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">d</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">W</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">d</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">t</span></span></span></span></span>。它是全 hub 的动机总纲，读完你会知道后面每一步在补哪个漏洞。</p>\n<p>第二篇《布朗运动》把这个抖动的对象钉死为精确定义：独立高斯增量、连续但无处可导、自相似。布朗运动是随机微积分唯一的「积分子」，后面所有积分都是对它的积分，所以它的性质必须先摸透。它与随机过程 hub 中的布朗运动篇有意呼应，但这里更强调那些直接影响微积分规则的路径性质。</p>\n<p>第三篇《鞅与过滤》给出证明层面的脚手架：过滤（信息随时间累积）、适应过程、条件期望、鞅（公平游戏）与停时。Itô 积分之所以是鞅、Itô 等距之所以成立、期权之所以能定价，全靠这套语言。它偏抽象，却是后续每一篇的隐形地基。</p>\n<p>三篇的顺序是「动机 → 对象 → 语言」，建议不要跳读。掌握之后，第二章「积分」才真正有地基可站。</p>\n"}